        "body-value": "What happened\n\nAt 09:12 the scheduler stopped picking up jobs. The queue grew for forty minutes before the first alert fired, because the alert watched the error rate and the scheduler was not erroring: it was idle.\n\nWhat went well\n\n- The rollback took four minutes once someone started it.\n- Support had a status message out within ten minutes of the alert.\n\nWhat to change\n\n- Alert on queue depth, not only on errors.\n- Write down who may start a rollback without asking first.\n- Rehearse the rollback once a quarter, so the four minutes stays four minutes.\n\nFollow-ups are filed against the Reliability project.",
